--- !u!114 &2185882073578702225
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2458990864075570831}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9fbae0ad507d0ec4c8e6a3695b3db864, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tools:
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  osciePickupDialogue:
  - So you're her, huh?
  - The only witch to ever flunk culinary school.
  - I've read your file-
  - Quite remarkable.
  - The dean wrote a letter of recommendation about you to the school of pyromancy.
  - 'Most examinees come to this forest for their final exam, '
  - grab a couple ingredients,
  - 'Throw em'' in a pot '
  - and grab that diploma.
  - Frankly, your credit total complicates that formality.
  - But don't worry, tadpole!
  - They have assigned you THE BEST,
  - MOST RELIABLE,
  - MOST SEXY,
  - MOST
  - uh most
  - MOST CULTURED!
  - Mentor and examiner in the whole department!
  - Okie croaky, Let's start this exam.
  - Go find some ingredients for a steak and chips.
  - Open your notebook by pressing TAB
  - Whatever the fuck that means.
  notebookFirstTimeDialogue:
  - Ok let's see what we're workin with...
  - 'On your left: the ingredients you''ve collected.'
  - Nice collection so far, tadpole.
  - 'On your right: The outline of a recipe.'
  - In the recipe outline, you can see each element of the dish.
  - You can also see what type of ingredients each element requires.
  - This exam will test your ability to sus out exactly WHAT ingredients and flavours
    should be in the dish.
  notebookFirstIngredientDialogue:
  - Oh look you got something.
  - You can hover over ingredients in your inventory for some info on them.
  - and click on them to pick them up.
  - (Metaphorically speaking.)
  holdItemFirstTimeDialogue:
  - Careful where you point that thing.
  - While holding an Item, press E to taste it.
  - Doing so will consume the ingredient, but will reveal one of its flavours.
  - You could try find spare ingredients to taste,
  - Or you could just throw shit in the pot and figure the rest out later.
  pickupToolFirstTimeDialogue:
  - Mm. Delicious.
  - You can learn a lot about a tool by its mouthfeel.
  - Observe-
  - or use scrollwheel to change tools if that makes more sense.
  pickupToolLastTimeDialogue:
  - Nice, another tool.
  - Now you should be able to gather all the ingredients you need.
  - When you've found everything you want, go back to the cottage and get cooking.
  correctRecipeFirstTimeDialogue:
  - Well, well, well...
  - Looks like someone vaguely knows how to make an adequate Steak and Chips
  - BUT
  - That's just the chip of the iceburger
  - You're gonna need a couple more dishes to pass this course.
  - AND INTERESTING ONES TOO!
  - I'm talking creative, innovative, magical shit.
  - We're gonna need better ingredients.
  - More than the staples you can find in this cozy forest.
  - 'Before that though, I have a memorandum from the committee:'
  - '"Thanks for playing the tutorial of our game. Spooky Forest DLC dropping on
    22 November."'
  - Huh.
  - Well that's lame.
  - You got games on your phone?
  chickenEncounterFirstTimeDialogue:
  - Those are some slippery clucks.
  - They seem to be scared by YOUR MOVEMENT.
